================================================================================================
(A) Prop 3.6(a),(b) in a small explicit class (PQ, one sample path)
    L_S = log C(64,8) = 32.04; class c-window of the rate-1/8 parity: (0.0175, 0.0507)
    lambda_n = sqrt(n) : MAP from n = 2^12 on: ['parity+rule']
    lambda_n = n^0.8   : MAP from n = 2^30 on: ['parity+rule']
    lambda_n = n^1.5   : MAP from n = 2^4 on: ['coin']
    lambda_n = 0.03 n  : MAP from n = 2^4 on: ['parity q=0.125']
    eventual MAPs: risk 0 under sqrt(n) and n^0.8; length <= l_min = 2 under n^1.5; a true-parity
    member under 0.03 n (inside the class's window); all assertions passed
================================================================================================
(B) Prop 3.6(c) at d=100, m=20, p=2^-10, B=30, delta=0.01, kappa=0 (illustration): c_hi(B=30) = 6.7357e-03
    [c1, c2] = [1.907e-06, 1.000e-04]: margin min(Phi_2 - J_g) = 0.3960; epsilon_bar_n < margin from n = 10^8 (epsilon_bar = 0.2031)
    [c1, c2] = [1.000e-04, 1.000e-03]: margin min(Phi_2 - J_g) = 0.3423; epsilon_bar_n < margin from n = 10^7 (epsilon_bar = 0.2119)
    [c1, c2] = [1.000e-03, 4.000e-03]: margin min(Phi_2 - J_g) = 0.1633; epsilon_bar_n < margin from n = 10^7 (epsilon_bar = 0.1305)
    so (c) applies here from n = 10^7 to 10^8 on, with a slack of 0.13 to 0.21 bits per sample in (ii)
